<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Saint-Aubin-du-Cormier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1488">1488</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mad-war">Mad War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Saint-Aubin-du-Cormier was fought on 28 July 1488 in Brittany and was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mad-war">Mad War</a>. A French royal army under Louis de La Trémoille routed the forces of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> of Brittany and his allies, capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-duke-of-orleans">Louis of Orléans</a>, the future Louis XII. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-le-verger">Treaty of Le Verger</a> that followed opened the way to Brittany's union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div>
